    {
      "text": "art thou come hither to torment us before the time, Matt. 8:29. can ye not discern the signs of the times, Matt. 16:3 (Luke 12:56). I say not unto thee, Until seven times: but, Until seventy times seven, Matt. 18:22. for the elect’s sake those days shall be shortened, Matt. 24:22. My time is at hand, Matt. 26:18. time is fulfilled, and the kingdom of God is at hand, Mark 1:15. ye know not when the time is, Mark 13:33. Jerusalem shall be trodden down … until the times of the Gentiles, Luke 21:24. No man hath seen God at any time, John 1:18 (1 Jn. 4:12). My time is not yet come, John 7:6. hath determined the times before appointed, Acts 17:26. knowing the time, that now it is high time, Rom. 13:11. when the fulness of the time was come, God sent forth his Son, Gal. 4:4. Ye observe days, and months, and times, Gal. 4:10. in the dispensation of the fulness of times, Eph. 1:10. Redeeming the time, because the days are evil, Eph. 5:16. of the times and the seasons … ye have no need that I write unto you, 1 Thes. 5:1. in the last days perilous times shall come, 2 Tim. 3:1. time will come when they will not endure sound doctrine, 2 Tim. 4:3. ready to be revealed in the last time, 1 Pet. 1:5. one day is with the Lord as a thousand years, 2 Pet. 3:8. keep those things … for the time is at hand, Rev. 1:3 (22:10). there should be time no longer, Rev. 10:6 (D&C 88:110). devil … knoweth that he hath but a short time, Rev. 12:12. woman … is nourished for a time, and times, and half a time, Rev. 12:14.",
